From 5c81225bbf7f4e27c2b6780dbcbbee8cc27bbb51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:49:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] ehci: run the isochronous finisher above real-time
 media threads

The isochronous finish thread runs the completions that queue the next
transfers (usb_raw streams requeue from their callback). At urgent display
priority the real-time threads of a media application could hold it off
past the queued transfers, and the endpoint went unserved for a few
milliseconds. On a Toshiba AC100 streaming 640x480 MJPEG, the microframes
that were never scheduled fell from about 1000 to about 300 per 5 s.

Signed-off-by: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
---
 src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
index 6dc38f230c..af6f28fce1 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/busses/usb/ehci.cpp
@@ -1409,8 +1409,12 @@ EHCI::_PrepareController()
 	}
 
 	// Create the isochronous finisher service thread
+	// Above the real-time threads of media applications: this thread runs
+	// the completions that queue the next isochronous transfers (streams
+	// requeue from their callback), and while it waits the endpoint has
+	// holes of several milliseconds that a camera fills with lost data.
 	fFinishIsochronousThread = spawn_kernel_thread(FinishIsochronousThread,
-		"ehci isochronous finish thread", B_URGENT_DISPLAY_PRIORITY,
+		"ehci isochronous finish thread", B_REAL_TIME_DISPLAY_PRIORITY,
 		(void *)this);
 	resume_thread(fFinishIsochronousThread);
 
